{"id":45979,"name":"Fond du Lac County","slug":"fond-du-lac-county","state":"Wisconsin","code":"WI","program":null,"sourceUrl":"https://vault.taxlienschool.com/tax-deed/tax-deed-states/wisconsin-property-investments-the-benefits-of-tax-deed-sales/fond-du-lac-county/","lastUpdated":"2026-07-27T13:28:55","facts":null,"bodyHtml":"<div class=\"yoast-breadcrumbs\"><span><span><a href=\"https://vault.taxlienschool.com/\">Home</a></span> » <span><a href=\"https://vault.taxlienschool.com/tax-deed/\">Tax Deed</a></span> » <span><a href=\"https://vault.taxlienschool.com/tax-deed/tax-deed-states/\">Tax Deed States</a></span> » <span><a href=\"https://vault.taxlienschool.com/tax-deed/tax-deed-states/wisconsin-property-investments-the-benefits-of-tax-deed-sales/\">Wisconsin Tax Deed Investments: The Benefits of Tax Deed Sales</a></span> » <span class=\"breadcrumb_last\" aria-current=\"page\">Fond du Lac County</span></span></div>\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-embed is-type-video is-provider-youtube wp-block-embed-youtube wp-embed-aspect-16-9 wp-has-aspect-ratio\"><div class=\"wp-block-embed__wrapper\">\n<span class=\"12isIljz3vpfCaGPDtohmUAgW4MESkLr0HyYZBTKwO5nRQVqF\"><iframe title=\"Beginner Tax Deed Investing (Step By Step)\" width=\"1170\" height=\"658\" src=\"https://www.youtube.com/embed/5RJylhmyFtI?feature=oembed\" frameborder=\"0\" allow=\"accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share\" referrerpolicy=\"strict-origin-when-cross-origin\" allowfullscreen></iframe></span>\n</div></figure>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-buttons is-content-justification-center is-layout-flex wp-container-core-buttons-is-layout-16018d1d wp-block-buttons-is-layout-flex\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-button\"><a class=\"wp-block-button__link wp-element-button\" href=\"https://linktr.ee/dustinhahnrealestateinvesting\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Click Here to Get Dustin Hahn’s Tax Lien and Deed FREE Mini-Course</a></div>\n</div>\n\n\n\n<div style=\"height:30px\" aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\"></div>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-yoast-seo-estimated-reading-time yoast-reading-time__wrapper\"><span class=\"yoast-reading-time__icon\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" focusable=\"false\" data-icon=\"clock\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" style=\"display:inline-block;vertical-align:-0.1em\" role=\"img\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-width=\"2\" d=\"M12 8v4l3 3m6-3a9 9 0 11-18 0 9 9 0 0118 0z\"></path></svg></span><span class=\"yoast-reading-time__spacer\" style=\"display:inline-block;width:1em\"></span><span class=\"yoast-reading-time__descriptive-text\">Estimated reading time: </span><span class=\"yoast-reading-time__reading-time\">6</span><span class=\"yoast-reading-time__time-unit\"> minutes</span></p>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Author:</strong> <strong><a href=\"https://taxlienschool.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"><mark style=\"background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)\" class=\"has-inline-color has-vivid-cyan-blue-color\">TLS Team</mark></a></strong><br><strong>Reviewed by:</strong> <strong><a href=\"https://taxlienschool.com/josh-blanchard-tax-lien-school/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"><mark style=\"background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)\" class=\"has-inline-color has-vivid-cyan-blue-color\">Josh Blanchard</mark></a></strong><br><strong>Fact Checked by:</strong> <strong><a href=\"https://taxlienschool.com/jack-aldous-tax-lien-school/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"><mark style=\"background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)\" class=\"has-inline-color has-vivid-cyan-blue-color\">Jack Aldous</mark></a></strong></p>\n\n\n\n<div style=\"height:30px\" aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\"></div>\n\n\n\n<p>Fond du Lac County sells homes and land that people lost after they stopped paying property taxes. If you want to buy one of these properties, you need to understand how the county gets them and how the sale works. This guide breaks it down in plain terms.</p>\n\n\n\n<div style=\"height:30px\" aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\"></div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-yoast-seo-table-of-contents yoast-table-of-contents\"><h3>Table of contents</h3><ul><li><a href=\"#h-what-is-a-tax-deed\" data-level=\"2\">What Is a Tax Deed?</a></li><li><a href=\"#h-how-a-property-in-fond-du-lac-county-ends-up-for-sale\" data-level=\"2\">How a Property in Fond du Lac County Ends Up for Sale</a></li><li><a href=\"#h-fond-du-lac-county-sealed-bids-not-a-live-auction\" data-level=\"2\">Fond du Lac County: Sealed Bids, Not a Live Auction</a></li><li><a href=\"#h-how-to-bid-on-a-property-in-fond-du-lac-county\" data-level=\"2\">How to Bid on a Property in Fond du Lac County</a></li><li><a href=\"#h-what-to-watch-out-for\" data-level=\"2\">What to Watch Out For</a></li><li><a href=\"#h-quick-facts\" data-level=\"2\">Quick Facts</a></li><li><a href=\"#h-faq\" data-level=\"2\">FAQ</a></li></ul></div>\n\n\n\n<div style=\"height:30px\" aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\"></div>\n\n\n\n<blockquote class=\"wp-block-quote is-layout-flow wp-block-quote-is-layout-flow\">\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"h-what-is-a-tax-deed\"><strong>What Is a Tax Deed?</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p>When a property owner does not pay real estate taxes, the debt becomes delinquent. If the taxes stay unpaid long enough, the county can take legal title to the property. This is called a tax deed. The county then sells these properties to the public to recover the unpaid taxes.</p>\n</blockquote>\n\n\n\n<div style=\"height:30px\" aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\"></div>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"h-how-a-property-in-fond-du-lac-county-ends-up-for-sale\"><strong>How a Property in Fond du Lac County Ends Up for Sale</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p>Property taxes fund schools, roads, and local services. When an owner skips paying for too long, the county steps in. Fond du Lac County uses a legal process called &#8220;In Rem&#8221; foreclosure to take the property. This is not a tax lien sale. The county does not sell debt certificates to investors. Instead, it takes full ownership of the property through court, then sells the property itself.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>Here is the path a property takes before it ever reaches a buyer:</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-table\"><table class=\"has-fixed-layout\"><tbody><tr><td><strong>Step</strong></td><td><strong>What Happens</strong></td></tr><tr><td>1. Taxes go unpaid</td><td>Owner stops paying real estate taxes</td></tr><tr><td>2. Certified letters sent</td><td>County notifies the owner and anyone with a legal interest, like a bank or lienholder</td></tr><tr><td>3. Court hearing</td><td>A judge reviews the case and grants judgment to the county</td></tr><tr><td>4. Minimum bid set</td><td>The Finance, Personnel and Economic Development Committee sets the lowest price the county will accept</td></tr><tr><td>5. Legal Notice of Sale published</td><td>The county posts the sale in the local paper, online, and at the Treasurer&#8217;s office</td></tr><tr><td>6. Sealed bids collected</td><td>Buyers submit written bids by the deadline</td></tr><tr><td>7. County reviews and awards</td><td>The county picks the winning bid or rejects all bids</td></tr></tbody></table></figure>\n\n\n\n<p>This whole process is backed by Wisconsin Statute 75.69, so the rules are set by state law, not just county policy.</p>\n\n\n\n<div style=\"height:30px\" aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\"></div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-yoast-seo-ai-summarize yoast-ai-summarize\"><h3>Key Takeaways</h3>\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list yoast-ai-summarize-list\">\n<li>Fond du Lac County sells properties through In Rem foreclosure when owners fail to pay taxes.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>The property sale involves a series of steps including legal notification and sealed bid collection, not a live auction.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Bidders must carefully research properties and follow specific steps, including submitting sealed bids by a deadline.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Properties sell as-is, which includes potential hidden issues and no guarantees from the county.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>For more information, check the Fond du Lac County Treasurer&#8217;s website regarding tax foreclosure sales.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n\n\n<div style=\"height:30px\" aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\"></div>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"h-fond-du-lac-county-sealed-bids-not-a-live-auction\"><strong><strong>Fond du Lac County: Sealed Bids, Not a Live Auction</strong></strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p>A lot of people expect a loud auction room with paddles in the air. That is not how Fond du Lac County does it. The county collects sealed bids instead. You write down your offer and send it in before the deadline. Nobody sees other bids until the county opens them all at once. Under state law, the county cannot accept any bid below the published minimum. And the county keeps the right to turn down every bid if none of them work in the county&#8217;s favor.</p>\n\n\n\n<div style=\"height:30px\" aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\"></div>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"h-how-to-bid-on-a-property-in-fond-du-lac-county\"><strong><strong>How to Bid on a Property in Fond du Lac County</strong></strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"schema-how-to wp-block-yoast-how-to-block\"><p class=\"schema-how-to-description\">Follow this order if you plan to bid:</p> <ol class=\"schema-how-to-steps\"><li class=\"schema-how-to-step\" id=\"how-to-step-1785186615331\"><strong class=\"schema-how-to-step-name\"><strong>Check the Treasurer&#8217;s page</strong></strong> <p class=\"schema-how-to-step-text\">Fond du Lac County posts current listings, bid forms, and sale terms under &#8220;Tax Foreclosure Sales&#8221; on the county website.</p> </li><li class=\"schema-how-to-step\" id=\"how-to-step-1785186636962\"><strong class=\"schema-how-to-step-name\"><strong>Read the Legal Notice of Sale</strong></strong> <p class=\"schema-how-to-step-text\">This tells you the deadline, the minimum bid, and any special conditions, like required repairs or demolition deadlines.</p> </li><li class=\"schema-how-to-step\" id=\"how-to-step-1785186651492\"><strong class=\"schema-how-to-step-name\"><strong>Research the parcel</strong></strong> <p class=\"schema-how-to-step-text\">Use the county&#8217;s Real Estate and Tax Data Search tool to look up tax history, ownership, and assessed value.</p> </li><li class=\"schema-how-to-step\" id=\"how-to-step-1785186666780\"><strong class=\"schema-how-to-step-name\"><strong>Check for other claims</strong></strong> <p class=\"schema-how-to-step-text\">Search Register of Deeds records for old liens that might still be attached.</p> </li><li class=\"schema-how-to-step\" id=\"how-to-step-1785186678650\"><strong class=\"schema-how-to-step-name\"><strong>Confirm zoning</strong></strong> <p class=\"schema-how-to-step-text\">Contact the local town, village, or city to check what you can legally do with the land.</p> </li><li class=\"schema-how-to-step\" id=\"how-to-step-1785186694576\"><strong class=\"schema-how-to-step-name\"><strong>Fill out the bid form correctly</strong></strong> <p class=\"schema-how-to-step-text\">Missing or incomplete forms usually get tossed out.</p> </li><li class=\"schema-how-to-step\" id=\"how-to-step-1785186710486\"><strong class=\"schema-how-to-step-name\"><strong>Submit before the deadline</strong></strong> <p class=\"schema-how-to-step-text\">Sealed bids go to the County Treasurer&#8217;s office at 160 South Macy Street, Fond du Lac, WI. Late bids do not count.</p> </li><li class=\"schema-how-to-step\" id=\"how-to-step-1785186722757\"><strong class=\"schema-how-to-step-name\"><strong>Wait for the decision</strong></strong> <p class=\"schema-how-to-step-text\">The county reviews every bid and picks the one that works best for them, not always just the highest number.</p> </li></ol></div>\n\n\n\n<div style=\"height:30px\" aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\"></div>\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-image\">\n<figure class=\"aligncenter size-full\"><picture><source srcset=\"https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/Fond-du-Lac-County-Wisconsin-Tax-Deed-1.webp 1081w,https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/Fond-du-Lac-County-Wisconsin-Tax-Deed-1-541x360.webp 541w,https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/Fond-du-Lac-County-Wisconsin-Tax-Deed-1-296x197.webp 296w,https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/Fond-du-Lac-County-Wisconsin-Tax-Deed-1-768x512.webp 768w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1081px) 100vw, 1081px\" type=\"image/webp\"><img src=\"https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/Fond-du-Lac-County-Wisconsin-Tax-Deed-1.webp\" height=\"720\" width=\"1081\" srcset=\"https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/Fond-du-Lac-County-Wisconsin-Tax-Deed-1.webp 1081w, https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/Fond-du-Lac-County-Wisconsin-Tax-Deed-1-541x360.webp 541w, https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/Fond-du-Lac-County-Wisconsin-Tax-Deed-1-296x197.webp 296w, https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/Fond-du-Lac-County-Wisconsin-Tax-Deed-1-768x512.webp 768w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1081px) 100vw, 1081px\" class=\"wp-image-45980 sp-no-webp\" alt=\"Fond du Lac County Wisconsin Tax Deed\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"  > </picture></figure>\n</div>\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-buttons is-content-justification-center is-layout-flex wp-container-core-buttons-is-layout-16018d1d wp-block-buttons-is-layout-flex\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-button is-style-outline is-style-outline--1\"><a class=\"wp-block-button__link wp-element-button\" href=\"https://linktr.ee/dustinhahnrealestateinvesting\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Click Here to Book a Call with Dustin Hahn</a></div>\n</div>\n\n\n\n<div style=\"height:30px\" aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\"></div>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"h-what-to-watch-out-for\"><strong>What to Watch Out For</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p>These properties sell &#8220;as is.&#8221; That means the county will not fix anything, and they do not guarantee the condition of the land or any building on it. Some parcels come with extra conditions, like a required deposit that gets refunded only if you finish repairs or demolition by a set date. Before you bid, always:</p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Pull the tax and ownership history for the parcel</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Search for unresolved liens through the Register of Deeds</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Drive by the property if you can, since interior access is rarely offered</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Call local zoning to confirm your planned use is allowed</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Set aside money for repairs, cleanup, or unexpected costs</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<div style=\"height:30px\" aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\"></div>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"h-quick-facts\"><strong>Quick Facts</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-table\"><table class=\"has-fixed-layout\"><tbody><tr><td><strong>Item</strong></td><td><strong>Detail</strong></td></tr><tr><td>County agency</td><td>Fond du Lac County Treasurer</td></tr><tr><td>Process type</td><td>In Rem tax foreclosure, then sealed bid sale</td></tr><tr><td>Governing law</td><td>Wisconsin Statute 75.69</td></tr><tr><td>Bid method</td><td>Sealed bids, reviewed after deadline, not live bidding</td></tr><tr><td>Property condition</td><td>Sold as is, buyer handles all research</td></tr><tr><td>Treasurer phone</td><td>(920) 929-3010</td></tr><tr><td>Treasurer email</td><td>treasurer@fdlco.wi.gov</td></tr><tr><td>Office hours</td><td>8:00 a.m. to 4:30 p.m., Monday through Friday</td></tr></tbody></table></figure>\n\n\n\n<div style=\"height:30px\" aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\"></div>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"h-faq\"><strong>FAQ</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"schema-faq wp-block-yoast-faq-block\"><div class=\"schema-faq-section\" id=\"faq-question-1785186478801\"><strong class=\"schema-faq-question\"><strong>What is a Fond du Lac County tax deed sale?</strong></strong> <p class=\"schema-faq-answer\">It is a sale of property the county took through court after an owner failed to pay real estate taxes.</p> </div> <div class=\"schema-faq-section\" id=\"faq-question-1785186494794\"><strong class=\"schema-faq-question\"><strong>Does Fond du Lac County sell tax liens?</strong></strong> <p class=\"schema-faq-answer\">No. The county does not sell lien certificates. It takes full ownership through the In Rem process, then sells the property itself.</p> </div> <div class=\"schema-faq-section\" id=\"faq-question-1785186505753\"><strong class=\"schema-faq-question\"><strong>How do I bid?</strong></strong> <p class=\"schema-faq-answer\">Submit a sealed written bid to the County Treasurer&#8217;s office before the deadline listed in the Legal Notice of Sale. Bids below the published minimum are not accepted.</p> </div> <div class=\"schema-faq-section\" id=\"faq-question-1785186521242\"><strong class=\"schema-faq-question\"><strong>Can I see inside a property before I bid?</strong></strong> <p class=\"schema-faq-answer\">Usually not. Most sales allow only outside viewing, since properties are sold as-is.</p> </div> <div class=\"schema-faq-section\" id=\"faq-question-1785186537186\"><strong class=\"schema-faq-question\"><strong>What happens if I win but do not finish required repairs?</strong></strong> <p class=\"schema-faq-answer\">Some sales require a deposit tied to repair or demolition deadlines. If you miss the deadline, you could lose that deposit.</p> </div> <div class=\"schema-faq-section\" id=\"faq-question-1785186552529\"><strong class=\"schema-faq-question\"><strong>Where can I find current listings?</strong></strong> <p class=\"schema-faq-answer\">Check the &#8220;Tax Foreclosure Sales&#8221; page on the Fond du Lac County website, or call the Treasurer&#8217;s office directly.</p> </div> </div>\n\n\n\n<div style=\"height:30px\" aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\"></div>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Sources:</strong></li>\n\n\n\n<li><a href=\"https://www.fdlco.wi.gov/departments/departments-n-z/treasurer/tax-foreclosure-sales\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"><mark style=\"background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)\" class=\"has-inline-color has-vivid-cyan-blue-color\">Fond du Lac County Tax Foreclosure Sales</mark></a></li>\n\n\n\n<li><a href=\"https://www.fdlco.wi.gov/departments/departments-n-z/treasurer\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"><mark style=\"background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)\" class=\"has-inline-color has-vivid-cyan-blue-color\">Fond du Lac County Treasurer</mark></a></li>\n\n\n\n<li><a href=\"https://www.fdlco.wi.gov/departments/departments-n-z/treasurer/department-responsibilities\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"><mark style=\"background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)\" class=\"has-inline-color has-vivid-cyan-blue-color\">Fond du Lac County Website</mark></a></li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<div style=\"height:30px\" aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\"></div>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Related Links:</strong></p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-yoast-seo-related-links yoast-seo-related-links\">\n<li><a href=\"https://vault.taxlienschool.com/auction-calendar-event/will-county-illinois-tax-deed-auction/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"><mark style=\"background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)\" class=\"has-inline-color has-vivid-cyan-blue-color\">Will  County IL – Tax Deed Auction</mark></a></li>\n\n\n\n<li><a href=\"https://vault.taxlienschool.com/tax-deed/tax-deed-states/washington-state-tax-deed-sale/jefferson-county/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"><mark style=\"background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)\" class=\"has-inline-color has-vivid-cyan-blue-color\">Jefferson County</mark></a></li>\n\n\n\n<li><a href=\"https://vault.taxlienschool.com/auction-calendar-event/jackson-county-florida-tax-lien-auction/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"><mark style=\"background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)\" class=\"has-inline-color has-vivid-cyan-blue-color\">Jackson County FL – Tax Lien Auction</mark></a></li>\n\n\n\n<li><a href=\"https://vault.taxlienschool.com/auction-calendar-event/orange-county-california-tax-deed-auction/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"><mark style=\"background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)\" class=\"has-inline-color has-vivid-cyan-blue-color\">Orange County CA – Tax Deed Auction</mark></a></li>\n\n\n\n<li><a href=\"https://vault.taxlienschool.com/auction-calendar-event/jefferson-county-washington-tax-deed-auction/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"><mark style=\"background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)\" class=\"has-inline-color has-vivid-cyan-blue-color\">Jefferson County WA – Tax Deed Auction</mark></a></li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<p></p>\n<p><em>Sign up or log in to view the full content.</em></p><div id=\"popup-overlay\"></div><div id=\"signup-popup\" style=\"text-align: center; padding: 20px;\"><h4>Get Instant Free Access To The Training Vault Now</h4><p>Learn how to get 18-36% returns on your investment and buy property for as little as $500 with tax lien and tax deeds.</p><div class=\"video-container\" style=\"display: flex; justify-content: center; margin: 20px 0;\"><iframe src=\"https://youtube.com/embed/FkB-M8RaSHo\" allowfullscreen style=\"width: 100%; max-width: 560px; height: 315px; border: none; border-radius: 8px;\"></iframe></div><div class=\"button-container\" style=\"display: flex; flex-direction: column; align-items: center; gap: 10px;\"><button style=\"padding: 10px 20px; font-size: 16px; cursor: pointer;\">Sign Up for FREE Access</button><button style=\"padding: 10px 20px; font-size: 16px; cursor: pointer;\">Already a Member? Login</button></div></div>","upcomingCount":0}